# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend — local development
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and adjust. All variables are optional.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the API lives. Leave empty to use same-origin `/api/...`, which is what
# the Vite dev proxy (`server.proxy` in vite.config.ts) and the production
# reverse proxy expect. Set an absolute URL only when the API is on another host
# (then that host must allow this origin via BACKEND_CORS_ORIGINS).
# VITE_API_URL=

# 1 = in-memory demo transport (seeded filings, canned cited answers, no backend)
# 0 = real backend
# unset = mock during `vite dev`, real for a production build
# VITE_USE_MOCK=0

# Dev-proxy target for /api/* (default: http://127.0.0.1:8000)
# VITE_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:8000
